disable bridgev2's "backfill thread inside backfill" pass.

FetchMessages ignores params.ThreadRoot, so bridgev2's thread backfill
resolves to GetPostsAfter(threadRoot) and receives the whole channel
window after the thread root as if it were "the thread". Every post in
that window that was already backfilled is sent to Matrix a second time
(the later Message.Insert fails with a UNIQUE violation, so the bridge
DB stays right but the room fills with duplicates: observed up to 26
copies of a message in a busy channel, 27 rooms / ~8k duplicate events,
2026-10-22 incident).

This fork models Mattermost threads as ordinary reply events
(m.in_reply_to) and thread replies are already part of the channel post
list the main backfill path fetches, so a separate thread pass is not
needed at all: clearing the flag makes bridgev2 skip it.

--- a/pkg/connector/backfill.go
+++ b/pkg/connector/backfill.go
@@ -79,10 +79,6 @@
 			ID:        MakeMessageID(post.Id),
 			Timestamp: time.UnixMilli(post.CreateAt),
 		}
 
-		if post.RootId != "" {
-			msg.ShouldBackfillThread = true
-		}
-
 		messages = append(messages, msg)
 	}
 
